    {
      "id": "IDU-01",
      "title": "A common integrality test for a row and two columns",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-duality",
      "statement": "Over the valued field of the unramified inert unitary model, suppose U,V,C,gC are integral, (U+Vg)C=I and the column b is the negative conjugate reversal of the row r. For every field scalar λ, λrC is integral if and only if λ(CVg)b and λ(gCU)b are both integral. In particular the least nonnegative denominator exponent d(rC) equals the maximum of the two column exponents. Including the two outer pure coordinates gives the denominator exponent max(0,a,d(rC)).",
