      "status": "independently reviewed",
      "correspondence": "The duality supplier decomposes r using C(U+Vg)=I and applies conjugate reversal to get b=x+g⁻¹y. Its converse writes b=w+g⁻¹z, uses the adjoint identity and the integrality of C and gC. The pointwise length proof applies the equivalence with λ=ϖ^(max(a,0)+k) and uses failure at the preceding level to locate a coordinate attaining the sharp bound.",
      "review": "The reverse formula rC=−w♯C−z♯(gC), its matrix order and the two explicit substitutions were independently checked against DualInterEqSum 99–111. The forward decomposition and the threshold from the two outer coordinates were also checked against their respective supplier and caller."
